## What to do

1. Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root, the linked plan in `docs/plans/`, and `.agents/skills/e2e-verify/SKILL.md` when installed.
2. Gather the acceptance criteria and changed user-facing routes or flows from the brief, git diff (`git diff origin/main...HEAD`), or PR description (`gh pr view <PR> --json title,body,files` when available).
3. Run the E2E verification suite from the repo root:
   ```bash
   node .agents/skills/e2e-verify/scripts/e2e-verify.mjs
   ```
   (or pass a specific Playwright spec after `--`, for example `node .agents/skills/e2e-verify/scripts/e2e-verify.mjs -- <spec>`). The script boots a throwaway database, runs migrations and seed, builds and boots the production app, and executes the Playwright suite (`E2E_TEST_COMMAND`) with `E2E_BASE_URL` and `E2E_ARTIFACT_DIR` set so specs save full-page state screenshots (`01-<state>.png`, `02-<state>.png`, ...).
4. After `e2e-verify: PASS`, open **every** screenshot printed in the output using your multimodal file-reading tool (`Read` / `view_file`) and inspect the rendered pixels against the checklist below.
5. Produce a structured verification report with embedded or attached screenshots.

## Inspection Checklist

### Mobile viewport & layout
- [ ] Mobile device emulation (390x844 viewport with touch enabled in `playwright.config.ts`) renders cleanly at every key state
- [ ] Card borders, containers and sticky headers or footers are intact with no clipping or overlapping elements
- [ ] Zero unintended horizontal overflow across all captured screens
- [ ] Primary actions sit within natural thumb reach without being obscured by fixed bars

### Touch targets & interaction
- [ ] Every interactive control (buttons, links, inputs, tabs, toggles) meets the >= 44px touch target minimum

### Contrast & visual hierarchy
- [ ] Text, badges, status pills and form controls maintain legible contrast ratios against their backgrounds
- [ ] Empty, loading, error and success states are visually distinct and readable

### Copy & localization consistency
- [ ] All user-facing copy is consistent in language, tone, regional form of address, accents, and singular/plural agreement
- [ ] No raw translation keys, leaked template placeholders, `undefined`/`NaN` text, or untranslated fallback strings

